      {
        "id": 161181,
        "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
        "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-03-08T06:04:25.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"ketigid\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/9fc29f/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> ketigid:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I don't want to start a new thread, so I'll post here instead.I recalled the reason for officially printing Cleverest Legacy was given something along the line of \"Every Legacy promo is a different person\".However, with the latest 1million Freedom Five stretch goal on Kickstarter, this is no longer true. The \"current Legacy\" is represented twice.So, I guess it's alright to print Cleverst Legacy as an official promo now, right, right?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Not quite. &nbsp;The official reason for not printing Cleverest Legacy as far as I know was more or less \"He was only intended to be part of the ARG.\" &nbsp;While it's true that they said that they liked having every Legacy be different, I don't recall that ever being listed as the primary reason that he wasn't being printed.</p>",
