        "created_at": "2016-03-08T09:30:15.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Arcanist Lupus\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n Arcanist Lupus:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>ketigid wrote:</b><br><blockquote>I don't want to start a new thread, so I'll post here instead.I recalled the reason for officially printing Cleverest Legacy was given something along the line of \"Every Legacy promo is a different person\".However, with the latest 1million Freedom Five stretch goal on Kickstarter, this is no longer true. The \"current Legacy\" is represented twice.So, I guess it's alright to print Cleverst Legacy as an official promo now, right, right?\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nNot quite. &nbsp;The official reason for not printing Cleverest Legacy as far as I know was more or less \"He was only intended to be part of the ARG.\" &nbsp;While it's true that they said that they liked having every Legacy be different, I don't recall that ever being listed as the primary reason that he wasn't being printed.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>couldnt it be an alternate universe legacy? Or a great grandson? &nbsp;I understand it wouldn't push the story forward any but does Completionist guise? Guise might be an exception though…lol&nbsp;</p>",
